# shellcheck configuration for the scripts/ tree. install.sh is POSIX
# sh; cft-bundle.sh is bash. The CI gate (.github/workflows/shellcheck.yml)
# passes the appropriate `-s` flag per file; this config sets the
# baseline exclusions we tolerate repo-wide.
#
# Scope notes:
#   - SC1091 — "Not following external source" — we don't shellcheck
#     sourced files (install.sh sources nothing); safe to disable.
#   - SC2317 — "Command appears to be unreachable" — POSIX `&&` chains
#     in install.sh can trigger false positives when shellcheck doesn't
#     track the failure path. Disabled repo-wide.
#   - SC3043 — "In POSIX sh, 'local' is undefined" — only relevant if
#     install.sh ever uses `local`. Currently it doesn't (POSIX-clean),
#     but the flag is forward-looking for anyone who tries to add it.
disable=SC1091,SC2317,SC3043
